WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
At Sarnath, the Buddha
gives his very first sermon.

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.450
He speaks like a doctor.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.570
First comes the diagnosis.

4
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.050
Birth, he says, is dukkha.

5
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.130
Ageing, sickness and death are dukkha.

6
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.920
Being parted from what you love is dukkha.

7
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.700
Not getting what you want is dukkha.

8
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.890
But why would he say even your happiest
moments are a kind of suffering?

9
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.300
In this mission, you'll find out why
dukkha needs more than one English word.

10
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:32.040
Then you'll sort three types of dukkha,
and test them on everyday moments.

11
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.360
Your mission: find out why even
happy moments can count as dukkha.
